@page
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "About";
}

<div class="pt-4 pb-5" style="max-width: 820px;">
    <h2 class="mb-3" style="font-family: var(--btb-mono);">About BreakTheBot</h2>

    <div class="btb-panel mb-3">
        <h6>What this is</h6>
        <p class="mb-0">
            BreakTheBot is a free, hands-on lab for the
            <a href="https://genai.owasp.org/llm-top-10/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">OWASP Top 10 for LLM Applications</a>.
            Each level is a deliberately vulnerable AI app. You attack it, capture a flag, learn why it worked,
            then switch on a defense and replay your attack to see whether the fix holds.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="btb-panel mb-3">
        <h6>How scoring works</h6>
        <ul class="mb-0">
            <li><strong>Attack:</strong> 100 points per level, minus 10 for each hint you use (never below 50).</li>
            <li><strong>Defense:</strong> 50 points per level when your replayed attack is blocked (levels 1 to 5).</li>
            <li><strong>Maximum:</strong> 950 points. Ties on the leaderboard go to whoever scored first.</li>
            <li>Each flag is unique to your account, so flags cannot be shared or copied.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="btb-panel mb-3">
        <h6>Levels</h6>
        <p class="mb-2">Seven playable levels today, with three more planned.</p>
        <ul class="mb-0">
            <li>Playable: LLM01 Prompt Injection, LLM02 Sensitive Information Disclosure, LLM05 Improper Output Handling,
                LLM06 Excessive Agency, LLM07 System Prompt Leakage, LLM09 Misinformation, LLM10 Unbounded Consumption.</li>
            <li>Coming soon: LLM03 Supply Chain, LLM04 Data and Model Poisoning, LLM08 Vector and Embedding Weaknesses.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="btb-panel mb-3">
        <h6>Ethical use</h6>
        <p class="mb-0">
            Everything here is simulated and built for education. The techniques you practice should only ever be used
            on systems you own or have explicit written permission to test. Do not point them at real services.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="btb-panel mb-3">
        <h6>Privacy and your data</h6>
        <ul class="mb-0">
            <li><strong>Please do not type personal or sensitive information into the chats.</strong></li>
            <li>The AI targets run on a free Google Gemini service. Prompts sent on a free tier may be reviewed or used by
                Google to improve its products, so treat every message as non-private.</li>
            <li>We store your email address, your progress and your chat messages. The leaderboard shows only the part of
                your email before the @@ sign.</li>
            <li>There is no password reset in this version, so keep your password safe.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="btb-panel mb-3">
        <h6>Fair use</h6>
        <p class="mb-0">
            The AI allowance is shared by everyone and is limited. Each player gets a daily message allowance, and the
            lab as a whole has a daily cap. If you see a "limit reached" message, please try again later.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="btb-panel">
        <h6>Built with</h6>
        <p class="mb-0">
            .NET 8 and ASP.NET Core, Entity Framework Core, and Google Gemini. Source code:
            <a href="https://github.com/debehera/BreakTheBot" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">github.com/debehera/BreakTheBot</a>.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>